# ERC-D — Deterministic Boundary

## Description

This module introduces a minimal deterministic model demonstrating that a system may lose recoverability without losing access to its state space.

## Key Result

As internal constraint increases:

- The recovered state remains part of the system
- But becomes dynamically inaccessible

## Contents

- `ERC-D_deterministic_boundary.pdf` — paper
- `ERC_D_model.ipynb` — simulation
- `figures/` — supporting figures

## Interpretation

The model suggests that failure may arise when recovery processes cannot keep up with system demand within finite time.

## Status

Minimal model. Intended as a falsifiable starting point.
